# Internal working documents stay local; the shipped ones are allow-listed.
#
# This block is a trap and has already sprung once, on Grid: a document was
# written, committed with a message saying so, and was not on GitHub for a day,
# because it was not on the list and `git add` had nothing to add. Adding a
# document here is half the job — `scripts/doc-check.sh` asserts each required
# document is actually *tracked*, which is the half that catches it.
docs/*
!docs/00-PRODUCT-STATEMENT.md
!docs/ROADMAP.md
!docs/JOURNAL.md
!docs/FEATURE-BACKLOG.md
!docs/TOOLCHAIN.md
!docs/adr/
!docs/screenshots/

# OS / editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.log

# Node / React Native
node_modules/
.expo/
*.jsbundle
ios/Pods/
ios/build/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
.env
.env.local

# CI is tracked; the `docs/*` allow-list above does not reach it.
!.github/

# Build output and task cache
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# .NET
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
*.user

# React Native
apps/mobile/ios/Pods/
apps/mobile/ios/build/
apps/mobile/ios/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
apps/mobile/android/.gradle/
apps/mobile/android/build/
apps/mobile/android/app/build/
apps/mobile/.xcode.env.local

# Gradle and Xcode output from *any* module, not only the app's.
#
# A gitignore pattern containing a slash is anchored to the file it is written
# in, so every `android/build/` rule above matches the repository root and
# nothing else. `packages/tracking-native` is also an Android module, and 168
# of its `.dex` files, class files and transform caches were committed — 1.3 MB
# of build output that `git status` reported as clean, because tracked files
# are not untracked files. Unanchored, so the next native module is covered
# before it exists.
**/android/build/
**/android/.gradle/
**/ios/build/

# Local development tokens and the log of the server that seeded them. Both are
# written by `make round-trip`, both die with that process, and neither belongs
# anywhere near a commit.
.dev-tokens.json
.round-trip-server.log
.round-trip-server.pid

# Engineering standards for whoever works in here. Kept out of the published
# repository; the ADRs carry the reasoning meant to be read from outside.
CLAUDE.md
